{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '241,332p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | nl -ba -v241\"","aggregated_output":"   241\t\n   242\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   243\t\n   244\tMaking Layer-2a components reusable solves code duplication; making **Layer-2b/2c preludes swappable libraries** solves syntax-to-runtime coupling. A frontend like `yang.python` becomes parameterized by a **Semantics Descriptor** (`:yang.semantics/descriptor`) alongside its grammar and runtime profile.\n   245\t\n   246\t### 6.1 Level 1 vs. Level 2 library composition\n   247\t\n   248\t- **Level 1 — Ambient Library Projection:** Keep the frontend's native semantics (`py`, `js`, `php`) and link an external module (such as `clojure.core`) into its global/module namespace via `yang.call`. Value marshalling (or passing opaque foreign values) happens at the call boundary.\n   249\t- **Level 2 — Pluggable Semantics Library:** Replace the frontend's lowering contract itself with a compatible prelude library (e.g., compiling Python syntax against `clojure.core` + `clj` directly onto persistent Yin data structures and `clojure.core` functions with zero value wrapping or marshalling).\n   250\t\n   251\tLevel 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and what ambient modules are linked into scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules`).\n   252\t\n   253\t### 6.2 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   254\t\n   255\tIn keeping with `yang.frontend/validate` (`non-portable-path`), a semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (keywords, symbols, strings, integers, booleans, maps, vectors) — zero Clojure host functions or AST-builder closures inside the descriptor value. A small closed set of pure literal/hook interpreters in `yang.core.semantics` evaluates the descriptor deterministically across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   256\t\n   257\t```clojure\n   258\t{:yang.semantics/schema 1\n   259\t :yang.semantics/id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   260\t :yang.semantics/syntax :python\n   261\t :yang.semantics/prelude-module 'clj.py\n   262\t :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\n   263\t [{:module 'yang.call, :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   264\t  {:module 'yrt.escape, :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   265\t  {:module 'clj, :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   266\t  {:module 'clojure.core, :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   267\t  {:module 'clj.py, :address \"<blake3-address>\"}]\n   268\t\n   269\t :yang.semantics/capabilities\n   270\t {:mutation/locals    :cell          ;; :cell | :single-assignment | :refused\n   271\t  :mutation/subscript :refused       ;; :supported | :refused\n   272\t  :mutation/attribute :refused\n   273\t  :mutation/delete    :refused\n   274\t  :calls/positional   :supported\n   275\t  :calls/kwargs       :refused\n   276\t  :calls/varargs      :supported\n   277\t  :control/exceptions :supported\n   278\t  :control/generators :refused\n   279\t  :control/with       :refused\n   280\t  :oo/classes         :refused\n   281\t  :modules/import     :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\n   282\t\n   283\t :yang.semantics/literals\n   284\t {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n   285\t  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n   286\t  :str     {:kind :raw}\n   287\t  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n   288\t  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n   289\t  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n   290\t\n   291\t :yang.semantics/hooks\n   292\t {:op/add         '+\n   293\t  :op/sub         '-\n   294\t  :op/mul         '*\n   295\t  :op/truediv     '/\n   296\t  :op/eq          '=\n   297\t  :op/ne          'clojure.core/not=\n   298\t  :op/lt          '<\n   299\t  :op/le          '<=\n   300\t  :op/gt          '>\n   301\t  :op/ge          '>=\n   302\t  :op/neg         'clj.py/neg\n   303\t  :op/lnot        'not\n   304\t  :op/truthy      'clj.py/truthy\n   305\t  :coll/list      {:build :vector, :conj 'conj}\n   306\t  :coll/tuple     {:build :vector, :conj 'conj}\n   307\t  :coll/set       {:build :call-seq, :fn 'set}\n   308\t  :coll/dict      {:build :call-kv-seq, :fn 'hash-map}\n   309\t  :coll/getitem   'clj.py/get-item\n   310\t  :env/local-get  'clj.py/local-get\n   311\t  :env/global-get 'clj/global-get\n   312\t  :env/global-set 'clj/define-global!\n   313\t  :fn/make        'clj.py/make-fn\n   314\t  :fn/call        'yang.call/invoke\n   315\t  :ctrl/try       'clj/try\n   316\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj/try-finally\n   317\t  :ctrl/raise     'clj/raise\n   318\t  :ctrl/call-ec   'clj.py/call-ec\n   319\t  :unit/run-main  'clj/run-main}\n   320\t\n   321\t :yang.semantics/identifier-aliases\n   322\t {\"is_empty\"  'clojure.core/empty?\n   323\t  \"is_nil\"    'nil?\n   324\t  \"is_map\"    'clojure.core/map?\n   325\t  \"is_vector\" 'clojure.core/vector?\n   326\t  \"is_set\"    'clojure.core/set?\n   327\t  \"assoc_in\"  'clojure.core/assoc-in\n   328\t  \"update_in\" 'clojure.core/update-in\n   329\t  \"str_join\"  'clojure.core/str}}\n   330\t```\n   331\t\n   332\t### 6.3 Lowering contract, fail-closed validation, and address neutrality\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
