{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.core.module\n  \"Module emitter machinery shared by every language frontend\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L3): the linker module naming\n   rule, the `require` and wide-application tree nodes, free-name\n   declaration over a host registry, and the `module-spec` and SCC bundle\n   shapes `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` takes. A language supplies\n   its prefix, its runtime module and its module AST; nothing here knows a\n   source language.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.core.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.core.prelude-admission :as prelude-admission]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(defn module-symbol\n  \"The linker module name of source module `name` under language `prefix`\n   (\\\"py\\\", \\\"php\\\", \\\"js\\\"): `<prefix>m.` then the name with each dot a `$`,\n   so no linker module name is a dotted prefix of another.\"\n  [prefix name]\n  (symbol (str prefix \"m.\" (str/replace name \".\" \"$\"))))\n\n\n(defn require-node\n  \"(require 'm) as a tree node.\"\n  [m]\n  (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote m))))\n\n\n(defn module-tree\n  \"A wide application: all definitions remain at module level.\"\n  [operands]\n  (prelude/wide-app operands))\n\n\n(defn declare-free-name\n  \"The `:primitives` entry free name `n` declares over `registry`, or nil\n   when `covered` (the requirement-pinned module names) covers it. A name\n   no `vm/primitives` profile or host export supplies throws, with\n   `refusal` under `refusal-key` in its data.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry covered n]\n  (if (and (symbol? n) (some? (namespace n))\n           (contains? covered (symbol (namespace n))))\n    nil\n    (or (prelude-admission/host-declaration registry n)\n        (throw (ex-info \"the module reads an undeclared name\"\n                        {refusal-key refusal, :name n})))))\n\n\n(defn free-primitives\n  \"The `:primitives` map declaring every free name of `ast` over `registry`.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry covered ast]\n  (into {}\n        (keep (partial declare-free-name refusal-key refusal registry covered))\n        (prelude/free-name-vec ast)))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`publish-module!`'s spec for module `name`: `ast` with `exports`, requiring\n   the runtime module `runtime-name` at `runtime-address` and each of `deps`\n   ({module-symbol address}). A free name under a required module is covered\n   by it; any other is declared as `declare-free-name` does.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry\n   {:keys [name ast exports runtime-name runtime-address deps]}]\n  (let [requires (into {runtime-name runtime-address} deps)]\n    {:name name,\n     :ast ast,\n     :exports exports,\n     :requires requires,\n     :primitives (free-primitives refusal-key refusal registry\n                                  (set (keys requires)) ast)}))\n\n\n(defn alias-spec\n  \"A thin member alias of the SCC bundle `bundle-name`: it requires the\n   bundle and defines `spec` and `body` as the bundle's `spec-key` and\n   `body-key` exports.\"\n  [name exports require-profile bundle-name spec-key body-key]\n  {:name name,\n   :exports exports,\n   :primitives {'require require-profile},\n   :ast (module-tree\n          [(require-node bundle-name)\n           (u/def! 'spec (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str spec-key))))\n           (u/def! 'body (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str body-key))))])})\n\n\n(defn scc-module-specs\n  \"The SCC publication shape: the `bundle` spec first, then the member alias\n   specs (each `alias-spec`'s output) in member order.\"\n  [bundle aliases]\n  (into [bundle] aliases))\n(ns yang.core.publication\n  \"Language-neutral publication of a set of compiled units as linker modules\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L3; the Python instance is\n   docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6). A unit set publishes bottom-up: each\n   unit's static imports order it after the units it imports, and each is\n   published pinning the manifest address of every import. Cyclic components\n   are bundled into one unit with lazy member bodies and thin member aliases,\n   eliminating circular content pins. Name assertions stay the linker's: this\n   namespace publishes content, it signs nothing.\n\n   A frontend supplies a config map:\n   `:imported-names`    `(fn [unit])` -> the module names `unit` imports\n   `:module-spec`       `(fn [registry unit runtime-address deps])`\n   `:scc-module-specs`  `(fn [registry units runtime-address deps])`\n   `:site-set`          `(fn [handle address ast])` -> site publication, or nil\n                        (Python's I7 mark set; none for a frontend without)\n   `:alias-site-set`    publish empty alias occurrence sets as well, when true\n   `:binder-table`      `(fn [handle address ast])` -> table publication, or\n                        nil (frontend-supplied; Python passes none)\n   `:refusal-ns`        the namespace string of the refusal keywords\n   `:publish-fn`        `[handle spec]`, default `publish/publish-module!`.\"\n  (:require\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(defn- refused\n  [reason data]\n  (merge {:status :refused, :reason reason} data))\n\n\n(defn- components\n  \"Kosaraju's two passes, with immutable search state. Members are sorted;\n   singleton components keep the old depth-first publication order.\"\n  [names imports]\n  (let [names-set (set names)\n        edges (into {} (map (fn [n] [n (filterv names-set (get imports n))])) names)\n        reverse-edges (reduce (fn [acc [n deps]]\n                                (reduce #(update %1 %2 (fnil conj []) n) acc deps))\n                              {} edges)]\n    (letfn [(finish\n              [acc n]\n              (if (contains? (:seen acc) n)\n                acc\n                (update (reduce finish (update acc :seen conj n) (get edges n))\n                        :order conj n)))\n            (collect\n              [acc n]\n              (if (contains? (:seen acc) n)\n                acc\n                (reduce collect (-> acc (update :seen conj n) (update :members conj n))\n                        (get reverse-edges n))))]\n      (let [finished (:order (reduce finish {:seen #{}, :order []} names))\n            partition (reduce (fn [acc n]\n                                (if (contains? (:seen acc) n)\n                                  acc\n                                  (let [r (collect {:seen (:seen acc), :members []} n)]\n                                    {:seen (:seen r),\n                                     :groups (conj (:groups acc) (vec (sort (:members r))))})))\n                              {:seen #{}, :groups []} (reverse finished))\n            group-of (into {} (mapcat (fn [g] (map #(vector % g) g))) (:groups partition))]\n        (letfn [(order-group\n                  [acc g]\n                  (if (contains? (:done acc) g)\n                    acc\n                    (let [deps (distinct (map group-of (mapcat edges g)))\n                          next (reduce order-group (update acc :done conj g)\n                                       (remove #{g} deps))]\n                      (update next :order conj g))))]\n          (:order (reduce order-group {:done #{}, :order []} (map group-of names))))))))\n\n\n(defn publication-order\n  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the input order for acyclic units.\n   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n   publication step per SCC. External imports must be in `published`.\"\n  [{:keys [imported-names refusal-ns]} units published]\n  (let [by-name (into {} (map (juxt :name identity)) units)\n        imports (into {} (map (juxt :name imported-names)) units)\n        missing (some (fn [u]\n                        (some (fn [m]\n                                (when-not (or (contains? by-name m)\n                                              (contains? published m))\n                                  {:module m, :imported-by (:name u)}))\n                              (get imports (:name u))))\n                      units)]\n    (if missing\n      (refused (keyword refusal-ns \"unpublished-import\") missing)\n      {:status :ok,\n       :order (mapv #(if (= 1 (count %)) (first %) %)\n                    (components (mapv :name units) imports))})))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"Publish `units` into the content store `handle` over the host registry\n   `registry`, the runtime module pinned at `runtime-address` and each\n   import outside the set at its address in `published`, in\n   `publication-order`, per the config `cfg` (see the namespace doc). Answers\n   `{:status :ok :addresses {name address} :bundles {bundle-symbol address}\n     :sites {name-or-bundle-symbol publication}\n     :binders {name-or-bundle-symbol publication}}`, or the first refusal:\n   `publication-order`'s before anything is written, else the publisher's\n   with a string `:unit`. An SCC member alias carries no marks; frontends\n   may publish its empty set with `:alias-site-set`.\"\n  [cfg handle registry runtime-address units published]\n  (let [{:keys [imported-names module-spec scc-module-specs site-set alias-site-set\n                binder-table refusal-ns publish-fn]\n         :or {publish-fn publish/publish-module!}}\n        cfg\n        plan (publication-order cfg units published)\n        by-name (into {} (map (juxt :name identity)) units)]\n    (if (= :refused (:status plan))\n      plan\n      (reduce\n        (fn [acc step]\n          (let [members (if (vector? step) step [step])\n                known (merge published (:addresses acc))\n                deps (select-keys known\n                                  (mapcat #(imported-names (get by-name %)) members))\n                specs (if (vector? step)\n                        (scc-module-specs registry (mapv by-name members)\n                                          runtime-address deps)\n                        [(module-spec registry (get by-name step)\n                                      runtime-address deps)])\n                bundle (first specs)\n                result (publish-fn handle bundle)\n                emit (fn [acc k r ast]\n                       ;; a handle with no byte store (a stub publisher)\n                       ;; has nowhere to put a set; a backend failure is\n                       ;; a refusal, not a throw\n                       (if-not (:put-bytes-fn handle)\n                         acc\n                         (try (let [emit1 (fn [acc slot f]\n                                            (if-let [pub (when f\n                                                           (f handle (:address r) ast))]\n                                              (assoc-in acc [slot k] pub)\n                                              acc))]\n                                (-> acc\n                                    (emit1 :sites site-set)\n                                    (emit1 :binders binder-table)))\n                              (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n                                (reduced\n                                  (refused (keyword refusal-ns \"site-set-unpublished\")\n                                           {:unit k,\n                                            :message (ex-message e)}))))))]\n            (if (= :refused (:status result))\n              (reduced (assoc result :unit (if (vector? step) (str (:name bundle)) step)))\n              (if (vector? step)\n                ;; A member alias holds no marks: the marks live in the\n                ;; bundle. Some frontends publish the alias's empty set too.\n                (let [base (-> acc\n                               (assoc-in [:bundles (:name bundle)] (:address result))\n                               (emit (:name bundle) result (:ast bundle)))]\n                  (if (reduced? base)\n                    base\n                    (let [aliases (reduce (fn [a [n spec]]\n                                            (let [r (publish-fn\n                                                      handle (assoc spec :requires\n                                                                    {(:name bundle) (:address result)}))]\n                                              (if (= :refused (:status r))\n                                                (reduced (assoc r :unit n))\n                                                (let [a (assoc-in a [:addresses n] (:address r))]\n                                                  (if alias-site-set\n                                                    (emit a n r (:ast spec))\n                                                    a)))))\n                                          base\n                                          (map vector members (rest specs)))]\n                      (if (= :refused (:status aliases)) (reduced aliases) aliases))))\n                (-> acc\n                    (assoc-in [:addresses step] (:address result))\n                    (emit step result (:ast bundle)))))))\n        {:status :ok, :addresses {}, :bundles {}}\n        (:order plan)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.frontend\n  \"The language frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 3,\n   section 8.5.6 slice F1): manifest validation, `install`, and `select`.\n\n   A catalog is a plain immutable value. There is no global registry and\n   no namespace-load registration: `install` returns a new catalog and\n   never changes its argument, so an in-flight request that pinned a\n   catalog snapshot keeps its behavior (section 3.3).\n\n   A manifest is portable data only: no functions, host handles, records,\n   or other host objects anywhere in it (section 3.1). The installed\n   binding is the host's own value, kept beside the manifest and never\n   inspected here; its shape is the composition's (slice F2).\n\n   Revisions of one frontend id coexist (section 3.7): an entry is keyed by\n   `[id revision]`, and a revision is immutable once installed.\n\n   Every refusal is a returned data outcome,\n   `{:status :refused, :reason :yang.frontend/<reason>}` plus its evidence;\n   a selection is `{:status :ok, :manifest m, :binding b}`.\")\n\n\n(def supported-spi\n  \"The SPI revisions (`:yang.frontend/spi`) this catalog admits.\"\n  #{1})\n\n\n(def refusal-reasons\n  \"Every reason a catalog refusal may carry.\"\n  #{:yang.frontend/malformed :yang.frontend/non-portable\n    :yang.frontend/incompatible-spi :yang.frontend/revision-conflict\n    :yang.frontend/unknown :yang.frontend/ambiguous\n    :yang.frontend/incompatible})\n\n\n(defn refused\n  \"A qualified refusal: `{:status :refused, :reason reason}` merged with\n   the evidence `data`.\"\n  ([reason] (refused reason {}))\n  ([reason data]\n   (merge data {:status :refused, :reason reason})))\n\n\n(defn refused?\n  \"True when `res` is a catalog refusal.\"\n  [res]\n  (and (map? res) (= :refused (:status res))))\n\n\n(defn ok?\n  \"True when `res` is a successful selection.\"\n  [res]\n  (and (map? res) (= :ok (:status res))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Manifest validation (sections 3.1, 3.7)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- non-portable-path\n  \"The path to the first value in `x` that is not portable data, or nil.\n   A set member has no stable position, so its path ends at the set, and a\n   map key's path ends at its map. With several defects the first reported\n   follows host iteration order.\"\n  [x path]\n  (cond (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)\n            (number? x) (char? x))\n        nil\n        (record? x) path\n        (map? x) (some (fn [[k v]]\n                         (or (non-portable-path k path)\n                             (non-portable-path v (conj path k))))\n                       x)\n        (or (vector? x) (seq? x))\n        (some (fn [[i v]] (non-portable-path v (conj path i)))\n              (map-indexed vector x))\n        (set? x) (when (some #(non-portable-path % path) x) path)\n        :else path))\n\n\n(defn- address?\n  \"A content address: a `:segment/...` key or a non-empty string.\"\n  [x]\n  (or (keyword? x) (and (string? x) (seq x))))\n\n\n(def ^:private manifest-checks\n  \"`[key valid?]` for every key section 3.7 pins per request. The spi is\n   `int?`, which on JavaScript also admits an integral float such as 1.0.\"\n  [[:yang.frontend/id qualified-keyword?]\n   [:yang.frontend/spi int?]\n   [:yang.frontend/revision #(and (string? %) (seq %))]\n   [:yang.frontend/language keyword?]\n   [:yang.frontend/grammar map?]\n   [:yang.frontend/options-schema address?]\n   [:yang.frontend/lowering-profile address?]\n   [:yang.frontend/runtime-profile address?]\n   [:yang.frontend/support-profile address?]])\n\n\n(def ^:private grammar-checks\n  \"`[key valid?]` for the grammar package. The lexer and parser names are\n   ANTLR's and optional, but a non-empty string when present: the SPI does\n   not require ANTLR (section 3.6).\"\n  [[:yang.grammar/package address?]\n   [:yang.grammar/entries #(and (map? %) (seq %))]\n   [:yang.grammar/export-profile keyword?]])\n\n\n(defn- optional-name?\n  [m k]\n  (or (not (contains? m k))\n      (let [v (get m k)] (and (string? v) (seq v)))))\n\n\n(defn- first-defect\n  [m checks path]\n  (some (fn [[k valid?]]\n          (let [v (get m k)]\n            (when-not (valid? v)\n              (refused :yang.frontend/malformed\n                       {:path (conj path k),\n                        :defect (if (contains? m k) :invalid :missing)}))))\n        checks))\n\n\n(defn validate\n  \"`{:status :ok, :manifest m}` when `m` is a portable, versioned manifest\n   this catalog admits, else the refusal naming the first defect.\"\n  [m]\n  (if-not (map? m)\n    (refused :yang.frontend/malformed {:path [], :defect :invalid})\n    (if-let [path (non-portable-path m [])]\n      (refused :yang.frontend/non-portable {:path path})\n      (or (first-defect m manifest-checks [])\n          (first-defect (:yang.frontend/grammar m)\n                        grammar-checks\n                        [:yang.frontend/grammar])\n          (some (fn [k]\n                  (when-not (optional-name? (:yang.frontend/grammar m) k)\n                    (refused :yang.frontend/malformed\n                             {:path [:yang.frontend/grammar k],\n                              :defect :invalid})))\n                [:yang.grammar/lexer :yang.grammar/parser])\n          (when-not (contains? supported-spi (:yang.frontend/spi m))\n            (refused :yang.frontend/incompatible-spi\n                     {:spi (:yang.frontend/spi m),\n                      :supported supported-spi}))\n          {:status :ok, :manifest m}))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Catalog (section 3.3)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def empty-catalog\n  \"The catalog with no frontend installed.\"\n  {:yang.frontend/entries {}})\n\n\n(defn- entry-key\n  [m]\n  [(:yang.frontend/id m) (:yang.frontend/revision m)])\n\n\n(defn install\n  \"`catalog'`: `catalog` plus `manifest` bound to the host's\n   `binding`, or the refusal when `manifest` is invalid or its\n   `[id revision]` is already installed with a different manifest or\n   binding. Re-installing an identical entry is the identity.\"\n  [catalog manifest binding]\n  (let [res (validate manifest)]\n    (if (refused? res)\n      res\n      (let [k (entry-key manifest)\n            entry {:manifest manifest, :binding binding}\n            prior (get-in catalog [:yang.frontend/entries k])]\n        (cond (nil? prior) (assoc-in catalog [:yang.frontend/entries k] entry)\n              (= prior entry) catalog\n              :else (refused :yang.frontend/revision-conflict\n                             {:id (first k), :revision (second k)}))))))\n\n\n(defn revisions\n  \"The installed revisions of frontend `id`, sorted.\"\n  [catalog id]\n  (->> (keys (:yang.frontend/entries catalog))\n       (keep (fn [[i r]] (when (= i id) r)))\n       sort\n       vec))\n\n\n(defn select\n  \"Select an installed frontend by `request`: `:yang.frontend/id`, and\n   optionally `:yang.frontend/revision` and any other manifest key\n   section 3.7 pins (SPI, language, grammar, profiles). Answers\n   `{:status :ok, :manifest m, :binding b}`, or a refusal:\n   `:yang.frontend/unknown` when no revision of the id (or the named\n   revision) is installed, `:yang.frontend/incompatible` when installed\n   candidates exist but none matches the pins, and\n   `:yang.frontend/ambiguous` with the matching `:revisions` when more\n   than one matches: the catalog never silently chooses (section 3.3).\"\n  [catalog request]\n  (let [id (:yang.frontend/id request)\n        revision (:yang.frontend/revision request)\n        pins (dissoc request :yang.frontend/id :yang.frontend/revision)\n        candidates (cond->> (revisions catalog id)\n                     revision (filter #{revision}))\n        matching (filter (fn [r]\n                           (let [m (get-in catalog\n                                           [:yang.frontend/entries [id r]\n                                            :manifest])]\n                             (= pins (select-keys m (keys pins)))))\n                         candidates)]\n    (cond (empty? candidates)\n          (refused :yang.frontend/unknown {:id id, :revision revision})\n          (empty? matching)\n          (refused :yang.frontend/incompatible\n                   {:id id, :revisions (vec candidates), :pins pins})\n          (next matching)\n          (refused :yang.frontend/ambiguous {:id id, :revisions (vec matching)})\n          :else (let [k [id (first matching)]]\n                  (merge {:status :ok}\n                         (get-in catalog [:yang.frontend/entries k]))))))\n(ns yang.clojure.prelude\n  \"The `clj` runtime module (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.10):\n   the published linker module every linked clojure program requires, as\n   `js`, `php` and `py` are for their frontends. It is written in prelude\n   notation and emitted with the same core machinery those preludes use;\n   it never runs on the host.\n\n   Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\n\n   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\n     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\n     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\n     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\n     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\n     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\n     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\n     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\n     standing);\n   - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\n     `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\n     allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\n     program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\n     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\n     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\n     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\n     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\n     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\n     module dictionary are the same seam;\n   - the continuation family, `clj/try`, `clj/try-finally`, `clj/throw`,\n     `clj/raise` and its helpers: the\n     `%capture` handler-stack scheme the py/ts/php preludes carry, over a\n     dynamic-context cell `clj.rt/ctx` (allocated by `clj/init!`). It is\n     the reference implementation yang.clojure's exception lowering\n     converges onto (R3, section 8.10.7); the consumer wiring that calls\n     these entries lands after the family exists;\n   - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\n     needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\n     adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\n     predicates read.\n\n   The module pins the shared calling runtime (`yang.call`) at the\n   convention's call-address, as the other runtimes do, and refuses before\n   anything is published when a free name nothing supplies is read.\"\n  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.prelude-admission :as prelude-admission]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module name of the clojure runtime.\"\n  'clj)\n\n\n(def runtime-keys\n  \"Every runtime key, each with an `:clj/uninit` placeholder at module\n   level so every read is discharged before `clj/init!` allocates the\n   real cell. They stay qualified: internal store keys, never guest\n   names.\"\n  '[clj.rt/state clj.rt/globals clj.rt/ctx])\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The module's definition list, in prelude notation (the module's own\n   `clj/` prefix is stripped on emit).\"\n  '[;; ------------------------------------------------- state and namespace\n    [clj/init!\n     (fn []\n       (if (= clj.rt/state :clj/uninit)\n         (do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))\n             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/ctx) (cell/new (clj/ctx nil)))\n             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/state) :clj/ready))\n         :clj/ready))]\n    ;; the runtime global namespace: one task-local map in a cell, keyed by\n    ;; export name. `clj/define-global!` answers the value, so a publish\n    ;; sequence can chain through it.\n    [clj/define-global!\n     (fn [name value]\n       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\n                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\n           value))]\n    [clj/global-get\n     (fn [name]\n       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n         :clj/unbound))]\n\n    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n    ;; The continuation family, mirroring py/ts/php (their preludes are the\n    ;; reference implementations): the dynamic context is one record in one\n    ;; cell, `clj.rt/ctx`, holding {:handlers} — clojure has no generators,\n    ;; no `with` managers and no recursion-limit hook, so there is no\n    ;; :depth/:base/:frame accounting the way py/php carry it. The handler\n    ;; stack is a chain of frames [tag payload rest n]: a :handler frame\n    ;; holds the continuation `throw` delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk\n    ;; of one argument (the thrown value, or nil) that every exit through\n    ;; it runs; n, the frame count, makes \"unwind to here\" an integer\n    ;; comparison. A first pass through a capture point is told from a\n    ;; re-entry by a flag cell, never by inspecting the continuation.\n    [clj/ctx (fn [hs] (assoc {} :handlers hs))]\n    [clj/rt-ctx\n     ;; the dynamic-context cell itself: `clj.rt/*` is an internal store key\n     ;; no closure of another module can name, so linked hooks read the cell\n     ;; through this export\n     (fn [] clj.rt/ctx)]\n    [clj/restore! (fn [saved] (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx saved))]\n    [clj/handlers (fn [] (get (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\n    [clj/set-handlers!\n     (fn [hs] (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers hs)))]\n    [clj/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (nil? hs) 0 (get hs 3)))]\n    [clj/frame\n     (fn [tag payload rest]\n       (conj (conj (conj (conj [] tag) payload) rest)\n             (+ 1 (clj/frame-depth rest))))]\n    [clj/pop-frame\n     (fn [hs]\n       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers (get hs 2))))]\n    [clj/raise\n     ;; deliver `e` to the current handler stack; with no handler above it\n     ;; the value escapes the whole stack (unreached in practice: the entry\n     ;; installs a top-level handler). A :finally frame runs its thunk with\n     ;; `e` before the raise continues.\n     (fn [e]\n       (let [hs (clj/handlers)]\n         (if (nil? hs)\n           (:clj/no-handler e)\n           (if (= (get hs 0) :finally)\n             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n             ((get hs 1) e)))))]\n    [clj/throw\n     ;; the guest `(throw e)` form: clojure throws arbitrary values with no\n     ;; wrapping, so it is `clj/raise` under the guest name\n     (fn [e] (clj/raise e))]\n    [clj/try\n     (fn [body handler]\n       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)\n             flag (cell/new :first)]\n         ((fn [r]\n            (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n                  (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :handler r (get saved :handlers)))\n                  (let [v (body)] (do (clj/restore! saved) v)))\n              (do (clj/restore! saved) (handler r))))\n          (%capture))))]\n    [clj/try-finally\n     ;; normal exit runs `fin` here; throw and escapes run it as they unwind\n     ;; through the :finally frame\n     (fn [body fin]\n       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)]\n         (do (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :finally fin (get saved :handlers)))\n             (let [v (body)]\n               (do (clj/restore! saved) (fin nil) v)))))]\n\n    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- entry\n    ;; The outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper is frontend-\n    ;; internal, so the entry removes one wrapper level from the\n    ;; program's value (a program returning that vector as data was\n    ;; wrapped again, so one level is exact). An error outcome passes\n    ;; through as the failure value for the caller to render.\n    [clj/unwrap-outcome\n     (fn [value]\n       (if (if (data/vector? value) (= (data/count value) 2) false)\n         (if (= (data/nth value 0) :yin.k/ok)\n           (data/nth value 1)\n           value)\n         value))]\n    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\n    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\n    [clj/run-main\n     (fn [body]\n       (do (clj/init!)\n           (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\n\n\n(def module-definitions\n  \"The module's definition list: an `:clj/uninit` placeholder for every\n   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n  (core/module-definitions \"clj\" :clj/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  \"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\n   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level. C1\n   finalized, like every production `yang.clojure` tree.\"\n  (yang/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The module's exports: every `clj/` key of the definition list, stripped.\"\n  (core/exports \"clj\" definitions))\n\n\n(def ^:private module-free-names\n  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the host\n   exports its manifest must declare.\"\n  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `clj` over\n   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call`\n   module at `call-address` — the convention's call-address, as every\n   runtime's publication carries. A free name nothing supplies is refused\n   before anything is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  [registry call-address]\n  (prelude-admission/module-spec\n    {:module-name module-name,\n     :ast module-uast,\n     :exports module-exports,\n     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n     :free-names module-free-names,\n     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n     :registry registry,\n     :message \"the clj module reads an undeclared name\",\n     :refusal-ns \"yang.clojure\"}))\n\n\n(defn register-library-module\n  \"Return `registry` with host module `name` installed over `entries`\n   (`[export function]` pairs) at `arities`, each export pure.\"\n  [registry name entries arities]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry name\n    (into {} entries)\n    (into {} (map (fn [[op _]] [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\n          entries)))\n\n\n(defn admit\n  \"Return `registry` with the guest library's host surface installed: the\n   `kind` module and the `portable` adapters of the data exports the\n   collection predicates read (yang.clojure's `library-adapters`). A\n   linked clojure composition registers them beside the other runtimes'\n   registry surfaces; a composition without a clojure program reads none\n   of them.\"\n  [registry]\n  (let [portable (into {}\n                       (map (fn [[source _]]\n                              (let [op (symbol (name source))]\n                                [op (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\n                                                          (get data/data-module op))])))\n                       yang/library-adapters)]\n    (-> registry\n        (register-library-module 'kind yang/kind-module yang/kind-arities)\n        (register-library-module\n          'portable portable\n          (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\n                (keys portable))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.core.prelude\n  \"Emitter machinery shared by every language's runtime-profile prelude\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L1). A language supplies its\n   module's own namespace string, its uninit sentinel, its definition list\n   and its refusal namespace; everything here is a pure function of those.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(defn define\n  \"`(yin/def (quote key) form)` in prelude notation: the key quoted, so\n   `sexp->uast` reads it as the literal symbol Rule R requires.\"\n  [key form]\n  (list 'yin/def (list 'quote key) form))\n\n\n(defn strip\n  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `ns-str`; any other value as it\n   is. Qualified internal store keys stay qualified.\"\n  [ns-str sym]\n  (if (and (symbol? sym) (= ns-str (namespace sym)))\n    (symbol (name sym))\n    sym))\n\n\n(defn- strip-form\n  \"A prelude-notation form with every symbol `strip`ped: references,\n   definition keys and quoted keys alike. Keywords, strings and the\n   keys of literal maps are untouched.\"\n  [ns-str form]\n  (walk/postwalk (partial strip ns-str) form))\n\n\n(defn- placeholder\n  \"The `[k uninit]` definition for runtime key `k`, so each read of it is\n   discharged by an unconditional module-level definition.\"\n  [k uninit]\n  [k uninit])\n\n\n(defn module-definitions\n  \"The module's definition list: a `uninit` placeholder for every runtime\n   key (stripped of `ns-str`), then every definition, stripped.\"\n  [ns-str uninit runtime-keys definitions]\n  (into (mapv (fn [k] (placeholder (strip ns-str k) uninit)) runtime-keys)\n        (map (fn [[k form]] [(strip ns-str k) (strip-form ns-str form)]))\n        definitions))\n\n\n(defn wide-app\n  \"One application whose operands are `nodes` (in order), applied to a lambda\n   with one parameter per node that returns nil. Every operand runs on the main sequence before the one call, so the\n   linker's scanners discharge every body read of a sibling or runtime key;\n   a `then` chain would nest definitions in closure bodies.\"\n  [nodes]\n  (let [params (mapv (fn [i] (symbol (str \"%d\" i))) (range (count nodes)))]\n    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) nodes))))\n\n\n(defn module-tree\n  \"The module tree for `defs` (`[key form]`, already stripped) followed by\n   the `trailing` UAST nodes.\"\n  [defs trailing]\n  (wide-app (into (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)\n                  trailing)))\n\n\n(defn exports\n  \"The module's exports: every key of `definitions` in namespace `ns-str`,\n   stripped.\"\n  [ns-str definitions]\n  (set (keep (fn [[k _]] (when (= ns-str (namespace k)) (strip ns-str k)))\n             definitions)))\n\n\n(defn free-names\n  \"Every variable name some occurrence of the map AST `ast` reads\n   unbound by an enclosing lambda.\"\n  [ast]\n  (letfn [(walk-node\n            [acc node bound]\n            (cond\n              (vector? node) (reduce (fn [a n] (walk-node a n bound)) acc node)\n              (not (map? node)) acc\n              :else\n              (case (:type node)\n                :variable (if (contains? bound (:name node))\n                            acc\n                            (conj acc (:name node)))\n                :literal acc\n                :lambda (walk-node acc (:body node) (into bound (:params node)))\n                (reduce (fn [a v] (walk-node a v bound)) acc (vals node)))))]\n    (walk-node #{} ast #{})))\n\n\n(defn defined-keys\n  \"Every literal key the map AST `ast` defines with `yin/def`, at any\n   depth.\"\n  [ast]\n  (set (keep (fn [node]\n               (when (and (map? node)\n                          (= :application (:type node))\n                          (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name])))\n                 (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\n             (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n\n(defn free-name-vec\n  \"The names `ast` reads and does not define, sorted.\"\n  [ast]\n  (vec (sort-by str\n                (remove (conj (defined-keys ast) 'yin/def) (free-names ast)))))\n\n\n(defn balanced-definitions->uast\n  \"Balanced definition-to-UAST emission: each [key form] pair maps to\n   u/def! and the vector splits at its midpoint, halving sequential depth\n   versus the linear u/seq-nodes chain. The tree shape is content-addressed:\n   empty input answers nil, and callers choose balanced versus linear\n   deliberately - never migrate between the two for style.\"\n  [defs]\n  (letfn [(sequence-tree [nodes]\n            (if (<= (count nodes) 1)\n              (first nodes)\n              (let [middle (quot (count nodes) 2)]\n                (u/then (sequence-tree (subvec nodes 0 middle))\n                        (sequence-tree (subvec nodes middle))))))]\n    (sequence-tree (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs))))\n\n\n(defn definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n(ns yang.core.prelude-admission\n  \"Constructs declarations/specifications and checks registries; does not publish, link, or execute.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn- refusal\n  [refusal-ns kind data]\n  (merge {(keyword refusal-ns \"refusal\") (keyword refusal-ns kind)} data))\n\n\n(defn host-declaration\n  \"`[n declaration]` for free name `n`: a primitive by its `vm/primitives`\n   profile, a host export `ns/name` by the profile address the registry's\n   host module `ns` publishes and its `:callable-effects` effect set; nil\n   when neither supplies it.\"\n  [registry n]\n  (if-let [profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives n)]\n    [n profile]\n    (when-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n      (let [entry (module/module-entry (:modules registry) (symbol (namespace n)))\n            f (get-in entry [:slice (symbol (name n))])]\n        [n {:yin.k/profile address,\n            :yin.k/effects (get (:callable-effects registry) f #{})}]))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for module `module-name`.\n   `skip?` (n -> bool) marks free names a requirement already declares;\n   `requires` is the requirement map. A free name nothing supplies is\n   refused with `message` under `refusal-ns` before anything is published.\n   This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  [{:keys [module-name ast exports requires free-names skip? registry message\n           refusal-ns]}]\n  {:name module-name,\n   :ast ast,\n   :exports exports,\n   :requires requires,\n   :primitives\n   (into {}\n         (keep (fn [n]\n                 (when-not (and skip? (skip? n))\n                   (or (host-declaration registry n)\n                       (throw (ex-info message\n                                       (refusal refusal-ns \"undeclared-free\"\n                                                {:name n})))))))\n         free-names)})\n\n\n(defn admit\n  \"Return `registry` when it supplies every one of `host-names`, else refuse\n   it before any program runs, naming each missing export in\n   `:<refusal-ns>/missing`.\"\n  [registry host-names message refusal-ns]\n  (let [missing (vec (sort-by str\n                              (remove #(some? (module/resolve-module\n                                                registry\n                                                (symbol (str (namespace %)\n                                                             \".\"\n                                                             (name %)))))\n                                      host-names)))]\n    (when (seq missing)\n      (throw (ex-info message\n                      (refusal refusal-ns \"host-names\"\n                               {(keyword refusal-ns \"missing\") missing}))))\n    registry))\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
