d naming, publication, provenance,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:244:### 2.3 Invariant enforcement\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:269:## 3. Language frontend SPI\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:271:### 3.1 Portable declarations versus installed implementations\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:323:### 3.2 Protocol shape\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:364:### 3.3 Registration and selection\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:389:### 3.4 Support profiles\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:409:### 3.5 Lowering contract\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:442:### 3.6 Adding a language without core changes\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:459:### 3.7 Versioning\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:475:## 4. ANTLR host boundary\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:477:### 4.1 One protocol, several deployments\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:521:### 4.2 Grammar discipline and per-host generation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:558:### 4.3 What remains host-local\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:588:### 4.4 Non-blocking interfaces versus synchronous parsing\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:610:### 4.5 ASCII policy and licensing\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:630:### 4.6 The multi-target pipeline and the parse-tree IR\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:695:## 5. Source ingestion\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:697:### 5.1 Source units are explicit\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:732:### 5.2 Encoding and source coordinates\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:757:### 5.3 Chunk boundaries: streaming by complete compilation unit\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:781:### 5.4 Backpressure, cancellation, and recovery\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:797:### 5.5 Portable CST packets\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:834:## 6. DaoStream integration\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:836:### 6.1 Explicit state and bounded work\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:874:### 6.2 Respect the existing outcome algebra\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:930:### 6.3 Admission and publication are distinct\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:954:provenance, and refs must all be retained before publishing a name, the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:958:### 6.4 Retention, duplication, cancellation, and restart\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:992:## 7. Universal AST encoding and provenance\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:994:### 7.1 Three layers, one authoritative content\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1004:3. **Datoms** `[e a v t m]`: naming, publication, provenance, diagnostics,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1036:### 7.2 Existing integration points\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1051:Phase 0 must settle the explicit conversion between provenance-bearing\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1059:### 7.3 Derive rather than duplicate\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1081:### 7.4 Provenance and fingerprinting\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1108:## 8. Semantic lowering per paradigm\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1115:### 8.1 Shared semantic foundation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1185:preserved within one transferred value graph, and the receiver mints\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1216:### 8.2 Placement of semantics\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1238:### 8.3 Paradigm summary\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1269:### 8.4 Object-oriented: Java, static typing and class-based objects\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1298:### 8.5 Dynamic: Python, indentation and dynamic values\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1318:  `yin/def` is reserved for the prelude and builtins. `exec` with a\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1356:#### 8.5.1 Python 3 mappability\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1527:#### 8.5.2 Safepoint insertion\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1634:- Inserted binders use a reserved `yang.safepoint/` namespace, with no\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1824:#### 8.5.3 Generators (phase C2)\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1960:advancement. Termination values are preserved for delegation, other\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2056:#### 8.5.4 Integers (phase C3)\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2279:  behavior are preserved. Comparison between an integer and a finite\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2365:  objects by ref) and the unhashable arm are preserved. The\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2529:#### 8.5.5 Float addresses\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2653:operator, operand position and the preserved printing.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2726:#### 8.5.6 Imports, the linked prelude, and the frontend catalog (phase C4)\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2795:| Base prelude        | `py` (reserved)                                        |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2797:| Hook prelude        | `pysp` (reserved)                                      |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2921:deferred, address verification and admission are preserved.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3035:  marks are preserved through publication and transformation, and loop\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3421:### 8.6 Object-oriented and web: PHP, mixed text and ordered maps\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3452:### 8.7 Prototype: JavaScript, lexical environments and jobs\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3479:### 8.8 Functional: Clojure and its hosts\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3489:### 8.9 Systems: Go, Rust, C, and further extensions\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3519:### 8.10 Shared function calling convention\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3528:#### 8.10.1 Decision and scope\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3558:#### 8.10.2 Callable representation and identity\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3598:VM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3654:#### 8.10.3 Invocation record\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3726:#### 8.10.4 Source semantics at caller and callee\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3780:#### 8.10.5 Values and projections\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3816:#### 8.10.6 References, higher-order calls, and ownership\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3841:#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3912:#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3946:#### 8.10.9 Publication, visibility, and reproducibility\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3975:existing provenance/unitarity rules. A fast path may omit the record\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3980:#### 8.10.10 Current code and migration\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4019:#### 8.10.11 Acceptance gates\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4084:#### 8.10.12 Cell-reference call routing and authenticity\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4151:### 8.11 Mutable objects and collections over cells\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4269:  reserved before contents are traversed; aliases and cycles inside one\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4270:  lift are preserved. One reference to one object pulls its whole\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4315:## 9. Standard library and FFI architecture\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4325:### 9.1 The four-layer model\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4351:### 9.2 Layer 1: pure modules\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4362:### 9.3 Layer 2: language intrinsics and preludes\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4395:### 9.4 Layer 3: object system desugaring\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4418:### 9.5 Layer 4: system I/O and effects\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4442:### 9.6 Module distribution\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4453:## 10. Diagnostics and error reporting\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4460:### 10.1 Boundary policy\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4480:### 10.2 Qualified outcome maps\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4494:### 10.3 Proposed diagnostic record\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4516:### 10.4 Diagnostic datoms on the stream\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4530:## 11. Determinism and isolation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4587:## 12. Phased roadmap\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4589:### Phase 0: SPI, ANTLR boundary, and stream pipeline\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4614:- No test relies on a reserved readiness extension or fabricated cursor.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4616:### Phase 1: Dynamic pilot, Python followed by JavaScript\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4665:### Phase 2: Java static and class-based pilot\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4685:### Phase 3: PHP web and associative-array pilot\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4703:### Phase 4: Language extension SDK and documentation (open SPI)\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4725:### Phase 5: Multi-host verification and integration benchmarks\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4754:## 13. Verification laws\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4756:### 13.1 Laws\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4770:   shares content identity while retaining distinct provenance.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4788:### 13.2 SPI compliance test matrix\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4822:### 13.3 Completion criteria\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
